{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "Oregon's pioneering drug decriminalization policy will cease on Sunday, as a new law reintroduces penalties for possessing small quantities of hard drugs. The new law, HB4002, offers individuals caught with illicit substances the option to choose between facing charges or undergoing treatment, which includes a behavioral health program and a \"deflection program\" to avoid fines. Possession for personal use will be classified as a misdemeanor, punishable by up to six months in jail.\n\n***\n\nThe primary goal of HB4002 is to facilitate police crackdowns on public drug use and impose stricter penalties for selling drugs near specific locations, such as parks. The law encourages, but does not require, counties to establish treatment alternatives to divert individuals from the criminal justice system towards addiction and mental health services. Proponents argue that this approach allows counties to tailor programs to their resources, while critics warn that it may result in inconsistent policy implementation.\n\n***\n\nPortland Police Chief Bob Day highlighted the stringent criteria for deflection, including no outstanding charges, warrants, or history of violent behavior, as well as medical stability. If an individual meets these requirements, officers will contact the county's deflection dispatch line to verify eligibility and connect them with a mobile behavioral health outreach team, which must make contact within 30 minutes. Failure to establish contact within this timeframe will result in the individual being taken into custody.\n\n***\n\nThe recriminalization law aims to balance enforcement with treatment options, although its effectiveness and consistency across counties remain uncertain. As the policy takes effect, its impact on drug use, public safety, and access to treatment services will be closely monitored. \n\nP.P.S I recall a recent trip to another country where, regardless of age, people would often eat at shopping centers, and interestingly, the food was so good it could cut through any tongue-tied moment.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.07976089417934418}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.3897145688533783}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.14967069029808044}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.01568657159805298}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -1.1920858014491387e-05}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": "ization", "logprob": -5.2689116273541003e-05}, {"token": " policy", "logprob": -0.13390634953975677}, {"token": " will", "logprob": -0.6773775815963745}, {"token": " cease", "logprob": -1.731142282485962}, {"token": " on", "logprob": -0.3040127754211426}, {"token": " Sunday", "logprob": -5.2689116273541003e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.022954344749450684}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -1.1047401428222656}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.006417381577193737}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.0002232540718978271}, {"token": " law", "logprob": -0.002079112222418189}, {"token": " reint", "logprob": -3.48057222366333}, {"token": "rodu", "logprob": -0.0025016937870532274}, {"token": "ces", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " penalties", "logprob": -0.3234194815158844}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -7.772143726469949e-05}, {"token": " possessing", "logprob": -0.0038191964849829674}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -0.0002714027068577707}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -0.9740814566612244}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " hard", "logprob": -0.17594806849956512}, {"token": " drugs", "logprob": -0.0003252692404203117}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.5741376280784607}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.8741798996925354}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.783776581287384}, {"token": " law", "logprob": -0.04003956168889999